-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Ikari Warriors
  Publisher   Elite Systems, 1988
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Ikari Warriors (1988)(Elite Systems)(48K-128K).z80
  MD5         54ad66af6678df22a9d4443e3d04aadb

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Players get bare skin with a red headband for player 1 and a
              blue one for player 2; enemies wear steel-blue uniforms with
              skin faces, so players stand out at a glance. A painted set,
              colourist not named.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz, the screen copy at 14 MHz
              or faster; works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11).

  Note        No outline on the figures, in both default and Enhanced: the
              owner chose that for this game. Known issues: the game reads a
              few ROM bytes as data and gets the Next ROM's values, not the
              48K ROM's (found by replay; effect on play not established);
              quiet scenes run 12 to 15% faster than the original in JNext, as
              in 1.0: the game has no frame limiter of its own, and holding
              them to the original's pace needs a pace limiter in the hooks,
              not in this version. Missing: no AY music, as this snapshot is
              the game's 48K form; the cheats are the archive's and have not
              been played; not yet checked: a level end and driving a tank;
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fuel
   3  Infinite ammo
   4  Infinite grenades
   5  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

